# Accounting Manual — Apps Script

## What this project is

Google **Apps Script bound to a Spreadsheet** (this folder, deployed via **clasp**). Source of truth: **`src/Code.gs`** + **`appsscript.json`**. Push changes with **`clasp push`** from this directory.

## Menu `📒 Accounting`

| Item | Function | Purpose |
|------|-----------|---------|
| Generate Workflow | `generateWorkflow` | Run only from **Business Summary** tab. Confirms, optionally invalidates sign-off, resets formatting, reads VAT + sheet picks, clears unprotected cells (except Business Summary), shows/hides tabs. |
| Sign off | `signOff` | Validates H5 + empty required fields, inserts log row, sets **F10/F11**, green tabs, builds hidden **Sign-off snapshot** sheet. |
| Re-initiated spreadsheet | `reinitiatedSpreadsheet` | Deep reset: delete snapshot, clear tab colours, hide all except Business Summary, delete Sign off rows ≥10, clear all unprotected cells. |

## Critical constants / cells

- **Business Summary** tab required for Generate Workflow (active sheet name check).
- **Sign off Page**: `H5` request gate; **`F10`** = latest log “up to date” (**Yes**/No); previous latest **`F11`** set **No** on new sign-off.
- Snapshot sheet name: **`Sign-off snapshot`** (hidden). Full-grid export; **font #ff9900** cells excluded (notes).
- OAuth scopes are explicit in **`appsscript.json`** (Sheets, UI, ScriptApp triggers, user email).

## Architecture patterns

- **Installable triggers**: `ensureTriggersInstalled_()` → `onSheetChange_` (sheet guard), `onSignedOffEdit_` (signed-off edit warning).
- **Sheet guard**: JSON snapshot in Document Properties; reverts hide/rename; **snapshot sheet delete** while signed off invalidates **F10** + alert.
- **Progress UX**: `progressStep_` / `progressDone_` use **`Spreadsheet.toast`** (bottom-right in Sheets) + short **`Utilities.sleep`** between steps.
- **Clearing data**: Prefer **`clearContent()`** to preserve data validation; **`resetUnprotectedContent_`** respects sheet/range protections.

## Agent checklist when editing

1. Keep **`SKIP_SIGN_OFF_EDIT_KEY`** around programmatic **F10** writes to avoid edit-trigger loops.
2. After adding/removing sheets programmatically, call **`snapshotSheetGuardState_(ss)`** so the guard stays consistent.
3. New menu actions: add to **`onOpen`** menu builder and implement with confirmations for destructive steps.
4. Re-run **`clasp push`** after edits; users reload the spreadsheet to pick up changes.
